  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">222938_FY24_WFP_Myanmar - Nutrition and Cash Assistance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The primary objective of the project is to enhance food security, nutrition, livelihoods, and disaster resilience in vulnerable communities through asset creation or renovation. Focused on 16 villages in Hlaingbwe Township, the project aims to strengthen the community&apos;s ability to meet their food needs and bolster disaster resilience and climate adaptation. This aligns with WFP Country Strategic Plan (CSP) Strategic Result 1, ensuring access to food for all. Additionally, the project seeks to promote gender equality by integrating gender considerations into the implementation of cash for asset interventions. Moreover, launching a &amp;#8220;Blanket Supplementary Feeding Program&amp;#8221; in Hlaingbwe Township, a region highly susceptible to natural disasters, particularly flooding in monsoon season. The crisis situation has left the community food insecure. The program&apos;s primary objective aims to prevent wasting - a severe form of malnutrition that increases the risk of illness and death. By providing targeted supplementary feeding, it could strengthen the resilience of vulnerable families and enhance their ability to withstand both food insecurity and disaster impacts. Through this initiative, lives will be saved, and the well-being of children and pregnant/breastfeeding women will be safeguarded.</narrative>
  </description>
